# Every file in this repository is owned by the business owner.
#
# Paired with "Require review from Code Owners" on `main`, this is what makes
# the owner's approval SPECIFICALLY required — not just any approval.
#
# Without this file, branch protection only asks for "1 approving review", and
# GitHub lets ANY collaborator with write access give it. Four accounts besides
# the owner have write on this repo, so two of them could approve each other
# and merge to main without the owner ever seeing the change. That is the exact
# thing the owner asked to prevent (2026-08-15).
#
# The owner is an admin, so he can still merge his own PRs — admins are allowed
# to bypass protection. Everyone else needs his review.
#
# Keep this as a single catch-all line. Narrower per-directory rules would mean
# some paths quietly fall back to "any collaborator can approve".

